From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gregordinary <33880035+gregordinary@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 01:00:52 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] debian: skip dh_shlibdeps, whose result the control file does
 not use

jellyfin-server's Depends are written out in debian/control, and nothing
there references ${shlibs:Depends}, so what dh_shlibdeps computes is
never used. The override meant to make it tolerant of missing information
was named override_dh_shdeplibs, which debhelper never calls.

In a cross build the step is worse than unused: dpkg-shlibdeps searches
the target's multiarch directories, which hold nothing unless the
target's libraries are installed as foreign-architecture packages, and it
stops on every library of the self-contained runtime it cannot find
(libc.so.6 first among them). --ignore-missing-info does not cover a
library that cannot be found.

Override dh_shlibdeps with nothing. The package's dependencies are the
ones debian/control states, as they already were.
---
 debian/rules | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/debian/rules b/debian/rules
index 353dbe6..7dcd0a3 100755
--- a/debian/rules
+++ b/debian/rules
@@ -71,5 +71,8 @@ override_dh_auto_clean:
 override_dh_installinit:
 	dh_installinit --name=jellyfin
 
-override_dh_shdeplibs:
-	dh_shlibdeps -- --ignore-missing-info
+# The control file names jellyfin-server's dependencies by hand and has no
+# ${shlibs:Depends} for dh_shlibdeps to fill, so its result would go unused.
+# Skipping it also lets a cross build run without the target architecture's
+# libraries installed beside the build tools.
+override_dh_shlibdeps:
-- 
